{"values": [{"id": 2011336521, "created_on": "2026-10-20T15:41:08.530420+00:00", "updated_on": "2026-10-20T15:41:08.550423+00:00", "content": {"type": "rendered", "raw": "what about `~/path` ? Is that considered absolute?", "markup": "markdown", "html": "<p>what about <code>~/path</code> ? Is that considered absolute?</p>"}, "user": {"display_name": "Vadzim Kavalenka", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/users/%7B804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550%7D"}, "avatar": {"href": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/VK-4.png"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/%7B804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550%7D/"}}, "type": "user", "uuid": "{804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550}", "account_id": "712020:91b25abe-63b7-4729-bde9-e440de77a1df", "nickname": "Vadzim Kavalenka"}, "deleted": false, "inline": {"from": null, "to": 49, "path": "amps-maven-plugin/src/main/java/com/atlassian/maven/plugins/amps/util/PathConfinement.java", "start_from": null, "start_to": null}, "pending": false, "type": "pullrequest_comment", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011336521"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011336521"}, "code": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/diff/atlassian/amps:ac98092cead5..f312c4e36b5f?path=amps-maven-plugin%2Fsrc%2Fmain%2Fjava%2Fcom%2Fatlassian%2Fmaven%2Fplugins%2Famps%2Futil%2FPathConfinement.java"}}, "pullrequest": {"type": "pullrequest", "id": 1255, "title": "AMPSDEV-373 Harden archive extraction and Spring Java transform against path traversal", "draft": false, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255"}}, "queued": false}}, {"id": 2011336826, "created_on": "2026-10-20T15:51:28.404028+00:00", "updated_on": "2026-10-20T15:51:28.421936+00:00", "content": {"type": "rendered", "raw": "Might not be important, but I can create files like `a:b.txt` at least in MacOS and they seem to be a valid file name, while it will be rejected because regexp recognizes that as absolute path", "markup": "markdown", "html": "<p>Might not be important, but I can create files like <code>a:b.txt</code> at least in MacOS and they seem to be a valid file name, while it will be rejected because regexp recognizes that as absolute path</p>"}, "user": {"display_name": "Vadzim Kavalenka", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/users/%7B804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550%7D"}, "avatar": {"href": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/VK-4.png"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/%7B804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550%7D/"}}, "type": "user", "uuid": "{804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550}", "account_id": "712020:91b25abe-63b7-4729-bde9-e440de77a1df", "nickname": "Vadzim Kavalenka"}, "deleted": false, "inline": {"from": null, "to": 37, "path": "amps-maven-plugin/src/main/java/com/atlassian/maven/plugins/amps/util/PathConfinement.java", "start_from": null, "start_to": null}, "pending": false, "type": "pullrequest_comment", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011336826"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011336826"}, "code": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/diff/atlassian/amps:ac98092cead5..f312c4e36b5f?path=amps-maven-plugin%2Fsrc%2Fmain%2Fjava%2Fcom%2Fatlassian%2Fmaven%2Fplugins%2Famps%2Futil%2FPathConfinement.java"}}, "pullrequest": {"type": "pullrequest", "id": 1255, "title": "AMPSDEV-373 Harden archive extraction and Spring Java transform against path traversal", "draft": false, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255"}}, "queued": false}}, {"id": 2011337003, "created_on": "2026-10-20T15:58:24.784158+00:00", "updated_on": "2026-10-20T15:58:24.802113+00:00", "content": {"type": "rendered", "raw": "This unpack archive twice. Doesn’t it? Would it make sense to do just one pass, validate entries as you go and fail when invalid entry is met?", "markup": "markdown", "html": "<p>This unpack archive twice. Doesn’t it? Would it make sense to do just one pass, validate entries as you go and fail when invalid entry is met?</p>"}, "user": {"display_name": "Vadzim Kavalenka", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/users/%7B804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550%7D"}, "avatar": {"href": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/VK-4.png"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/%7B804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550%7D/"}}, "type": "user", "uuid": "{804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550}", "account_id": "712020:91b25abe-63b7-4729-bde9-e440de77a1df", "nickname": "Vadzim Kavalenka"}, "deleted": false, "inline": {"from": null, "to": 83, "path": "amps-maven-plugin/src/main/java/com/atlassian/maven/plugins/amps/util/ZipUtils.java", "start_from": null, "start_to": null}, "pending": false, "type": "pullrequest_comment", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011337003"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011337003"}, "code": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/diff/atlassian/amps:e24b8a7a25dc..f312c4e36b5f?path=amps-maven-plugin%2Fsrc%2Fmain%2Fjava%2Fcom%2Fatlassian%2Fmaven%2Fplugins%2Famps%2Futil%2FZipUtils.java"}}, "pullrequest": {"type": "pullrequest", "id": 1255, "title": "AMPSDEV-373 Harden archive extraction and Spring Java transform against path traversal", "draft": false, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255"}}, "queued": false}}, {"id": 2011337148, "created_on": "2026-10-20T16:04:33.059809+00:00", "updated_on": "2026-10-20T16:04:33.081879+00:00", "content": {"type": "rendered", "raw": "but if it turns into `etc/passwd` doesn’t that become safe?\n\n‌", "markup": "markdown", "html": "<p>but if it turns into <code>etc/passwd</code> doesn’t that become safe?</p>\n<p>‌</p>"}, "user": {"display_name": "Vadzim Kavalenka", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/users/%7B804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550%7D"}, "avatar": {"href": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/VK-4.png"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/%7B804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550%7D/"}}, "type": "user", "uuid": "{804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550}", "account_id": "712020:91b25abe-63b7-4729-bde9-e440de77a1df", "nickname": "Vadzim Kavalenka"}, "deleted": false, "inline": {"from": null, "to": 256, "path": "amps-maven-plugin/src/main/java/com/atlassian/maven/plugins/amps/util/ZipUtils.java", "start_from": null, "start_to": null}, "pending": false, "type": "pullrequest_comment", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011337148"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011337148"}, "code": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/diff/atlassian/amps:ac98092cead5..f312c4e36b5f?path=amps-maven-plugin%2Fsrc%2Fmain%2Fjava%2Fcom%2Fatlassian%2Fmaven%2Fplugins%2Famps%2Futil%2FZipUtils.java"}}, "pullrequest": {"type": "pullrequest", "id": 1255, "title": "AMPSDEV-373 Harden archive extraction and Spring Java transform against path traversal", "draft": false, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255"}}, "queued": false}}, {"id": 2011383971, "created_on": "2026-10-21T07:45:42.171398+00:00", "updated_on": "2026-10-21T07:45:42.190629+00:00", "content": {"type": "rendered", "raw": "Good question! For ZIPs it's cheap: the first pass only reads entry names and modes from the central directory, nothing gets inflated. For tar.gz you're right, there's no index, so validating means decompressing the stream once more.\n\nThat's deliberate though. A single pass that fails on the first bad entry would leave a half-extracted archive behind, and `untargz` is only used by `atlas-update`, which extracts into the existing SDK home. Failing midway there would leave a mix of old and new SDK files, and cleaning up can't restore files that were already overwritten. Validating everything up front gives us all-or-nothing behaviour without a staging directory and a non-atomic move. The cost is one extra decompression of the SDK tarball per `atlas-update`, which felt like a fair trade.", "markup": "markdown", "html": "<p>Good question! For ZIPs it's cheap: the first pass only reads entry names and modes from the central directory, nothing gets inflated. For tar.gz you're right, there's no index, so validating means decompressing the stream once more.</p>\n<p>That's deliberate though. A single pass that fails on the first bad entry would leave a half-extracted archive behind, and <code>untargz</code> is only used by <code>atlas-update</code>, which extracts into the existing SDK home. Failing midway there would leave a mix of old and new SDK files, and cleaning up can't restore files that were already overwritten. Validating everything up front gives us all-or-nothing behaviour without a staging directory and a non-atomic move. The cost is one extra decompression of the SDK tarball per <code>atlas-update</code>, which felt like a fair trade.</p>"}, "user": {"display_name": "Frederic Ghilini", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/users/%7B2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e%7D"}, "avatar": {"href": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/FG-3.png"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/%7B2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e%7D/"}}, "type": "user", "uuid": "{2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e}", "account_id": "5b60ff90665a402d2a5a20cf", "nickname": "fred"}, "deleted": false, "parent": {"id": 2011337003, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011337003"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011337003"}}}, "inline": {"from": null, "to": 83, "path": "amps-maven-plugin/src/main/java/com/atlassian/maven/plugins/amps/util/ZipUtils.java", "start_from": null, "start_to": null}, "pending": false, "type": "pullrequest_comment", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011383971"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011383971"}, "code": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/diff/atlassian/amps:e24b8a7a25dc..f312c4e36b5f?path=amps-maven-plugin%2Fsrc%2Fmain%2Fjava%2Fcom%2Fatlassian%2Fmaven%2Fplugins%2Famps%2Futil%2FZipUtils.java"}}, "pullrequest": {"type": "pullrequest", "id": 1255, "title": "AMPSDEV-373 Harden archive extraction and Spring Java transform against path traversal", "draft": false, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255"}}, "queued": false}}, {"id": 2011384613, "created_on": "2026-10-21T07:57:29.504260+00:00", "updated_on": "2026-10-21T07:57:29.526383+00:00", "content": {"type": "rendered", "raw": "@{712020:91b25abe-63b7-4729-bde9-e440de77a1df} Thanks for your input! So absolute paths are now checked only on the final trimmed path using the current OS's own rules \\(`a:b.txt` works outside Windows and `etc/passwd` after trimming is fine\\), and I added tests showing `~/path` is never expanded.", "markup": "markdown", "html": "<p><span class=\"ap-mention\" data-atlassian-id=\"712020:91b25abe-63b7-4729-bde9-e440de77a1df\">@Vadzim Kavalenka</span> Thanks for your input! So absolute paths are now checked only on the final trimmed path using the current OS's own rules (<code>a:b.txt</code> works outside Windows and <code>etc/passwd</code> after trimming is fine), and I added tests showing <code>~/path</code> is never expanded.</p>"}, "user": {"display_name": "Frederic Ghilini", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/users/%7B2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e%7D"}, "avatar": {"href": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/FG-3.png"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/%7B2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e%7D/"}}, "type": "user", "uuid": "{2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e}", "account_id": "5b60ff90665a402d2a5a20cf", "nickname": "fred"}, "deleted": false, "pending": false, "type": "pullrequest_comment", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011384613"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011384613"}}, "pullrequest": {"type": "pullrequest", "id": 1255, "title": "AMPSDEV-373 Harden archive extraction and Spring Java transform against path traversal", "draft": false, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255"}}, "queued": false}}, {"id": 2011386118, "created_on": "2026-10-21T08:39:23.085560+00:00", "updated_on": "2026-10-21T08:39:23.106651+00:00", "content": {"type": "rendered", "raw": "@{5b60ff90665a402d2a5a20cf} Sounds good. Perhaps one pass solution would be to extract everything in temp directory and if succeeded copy to the target, but that might be an overkill", "markup": "markdown", "html": "<p><span class=\"ap-mention\" data-atlassian-id=\"5b60ff90665a402d2a5a20cf\">@Frederic Ghilini</span> Sounds good. Perhaps one pass solution would be to extract everything in temp directory and if succeeded copy to the target, but that might be an overkill</p>"}, "user": {"display_name": "Vadzim Kavalenka", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/users/%7B804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550%7D"}, "avatar": {"href": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/VK-4.png"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/%7B804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550%7D/"}}, "type": "user", "uuid": "{804c1c49-39cd-4290-bccf-dbb0d5ef3550}", "account_id": "712020:91b25abe-63b7-4729-bde9-e440de77a1df", "nickname": "Vadzim Kavalenka"}, "deleted": false, "parent": {"id": 2011383971, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011383971"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011383971"}}}, "inline": {"from": null, "to": 83, "path": "amps-maven-plugin/src/main/java/com/atlassian/maven/plugins/amps/util/ZipUtils.java", "start_from": null, "start_to": null}, "pending": false, "type": "pullrequest_comment", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011386118"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011386118"}, "code": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/diff/atlassian/amps:e24b8a7a25dc..f312c4e36b5f?path=amps-maven-plugin%2Fsrc%2Fmain%2Fjava%2Fcom%2Fatlassian%2Fmaven%2Fplugins%2Famps%2Futil%2FZipUtils.java"}}, "pullrequest": {"type": "pullrequest", "id": 1255, "title": "AMPSDEV-373 Harden archive extraction and Spring Java transform against path traversal", "draft": false, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255"}}, "queued": false}}, {"id": 2011387910, "created_on": "2026-10-21T09:33:10.428185+00:00", "updated_on": "2026-10-21T09:33:10.444808+00:00", "content": {"type": "rendered", "raw": "Pulling @{557057:6c7fbc05-b9ea-4fa9-b3da-482f3548cb76} for a sanity check, as i’m planning to push that change tomorrow ", "markup": "markdown", "html": "<p>Pulling <span class=\"ap-mention\" data-atlassian-id=\"557057:6c7fbc05-b9ea-4fa9-b3da-482f3548cb76\">@Brent P</span> for a sanity check, as i’m planning to push that change tomorrow </p>"}, "user": {"display_name": "Frederic Ghilini", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/users/%7B2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e%7D"}, "avatar": {"href": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/FG-3.png"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/%7B2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e%7D/"}}, "type": "user", "uuid": "{2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e}", "account_id": "5b60ff90665a402d2a5a20cf", "nickname": "fred"}, "deleted": false, "pending": false, "type": "pullrequest_comment", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011387910"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011387910"}}, "pullrequest": {"type": "pullrequest", "id": 1255, "title": "AMPSDEV-373 Harden archive extraction and Spring Java transform against path traversal", "draft": false, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255"}}, "queued": false}}, {"id": 2011408121, "created_on": "2026-10-21T21:52:11.559531+00:00", "updated_on": "2026-10-21T21:52:11.559531+00:00", "content": {"type": "rendered", "raw": "LGTM.\n\nIf you haven’t already, could you ask an LLM \\(one of the good ones… Astra or Fable\\) to look over this, too? I know it was probably generated with an LLM, but I think it’s worth having an adversary LLM evaluate this solution. `requireSimpleResourceName` is probably the biggest concern for me. In the HOT that spawned all this, we learned that looking for `..` and `/` wasn’t enough. That was in an HTML world, but unicode is full of surprises and `getResourceAsStream` may also allow some patterns we didn’t think of.", "markup": "markdown", "html": "<p>LGTM.</p>\n<p>If you haven’t already, could you ask an LLM (one of the good ones… Astra or Fable) to look over this, too? I know it was probably generated with an LLM, but I think it’s worth having an adversary LLM evaluate this solution. <code>requireSimpleResourceName</code> is probably the biggest concern for me. In the HOT that spawned all this, we learned that looking for <code>..</code> and <code>/</code> wasn’t enough. That was in an HTML world, but unicode is full of surprises and <code>getResourceAsStream</code> may also allow some patterns we didn’t think of.</p>"}, "user": {"display_name": "Brent P", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/users/%7Bfe8d1dd7-82d3-490b-9154-54e24011be4f%7D"}, "avatar": {"href": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557057:6c7fbc05-b9ea-4fa9-b3da-482f3548cb76/d9b6f99e-0334-423c-afa7-92d0fa45685b/128"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/%7Bfe8d1dd7-82d3-490b-9154-54e24011be4f%7D/"}}, "type": "user", "uuid": "{fe8d1dd7-82d3-490b-9154-54e24011be4f}", "account_id": "557057:6c7fbc05-b9ea-4fa9-b3da-482f3548cb76", "nickname": "Brent P"}, "deleted": false, "pending": false, "type": "pullrequest_comment", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011408121"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011408121"}}, "pullrequest": {"type": "pullrequest", "id": 1255, "title": "AMPSDEV-373 Harden archive extraction and Spring Java transform against path traversal", "draft": false, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255"}}, "queued": false}}, {"id": 2011439605, "created_on": "2026-10-22T07:51:03.720181+00:00", "updated_on": "2026-10-22T07:51:03.745124+00:00", "content": {"type": "rendered", "raw": "I did a last “beefy” run through Astra, and I was suggested this additional change that makes sense to me [https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/commits/e24b8a7a25dc3c72ec6c638c0bee151a75a37334](https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/commits/e24b8a7a25dc3c72ec6c638c0bee151a75a37334){: data-inline-card='' }   \n  \n@{712020:91b25abe-63b7-4729-bde9-e440de77a1df} @{712020:3fee4208-f33f-4f47-9709-246721c0d560} does that look good to you? I’d merge in that state and publish another AMPS version.", "markup": "markdown", "html": "<p>I did a last “beefy” run through Astra, and I was suggested this additional change that makes sense to me <a data-inline-card=\"\" data-is-external-link=\"true\" href=\"https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/commits/e24b8a7a25dc3c72ec6c638c0bee151a75a37334\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/commits/e24b8a7a25dc3c72ec6c638c0bee151a75a37334</a>   </p>\n<p><span class=\"ap-mention\" data-atlassian-id=\"712020:91b25abe-63b7-4729-bde9-e440de77a1df\">@Vadzim Kavalenka</span> <span class=\"ap-mention\" data-atlassian-id=\"712020:3fee4208-f33f-4f47-9709-246721c0d560\">@Etienne Lacazedieu</span> does that look good to you? I’d merge in that state and publish another AMPS version.</p>"}, "user": {"display_name": "Frederic Ghilini", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/users/%7B2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e%7D"}, "avatar": {"href": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/FG-3.png"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/%7B2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e%7D/"}}, "type": "user", "uuid": "{2e915df4-a4a2-4abc-9980-4110afef717e}", "account_id": "5b60ff90665a402d2a5a20cf", "nickname": "fred"}, "deleted": false, "parent": {"id": 2011408121, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011408121"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011408121"}}}, "pending": false, "type": "pullrequest_comment", "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255/comments/2011439605"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255/_/diff#comment-2011439605"}}, "pullrequest": {"type": "pullrequest", "id": 1255, "title": "AMPSDEV-373 Harden archive extraction and Spring Java transform against path traversal", "draft": false, "links": {"self": {"href": "https://api.bitbucket.org/2.0/repositories/atlassian/amps/pullrequests/1255"}, "html": {"href": "https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/amps/pull-requests/1255"}}, "queued": false}}], "pagelen": 50, "size": 10, "page": 1}